{"kind":"report","text":"Read-only clone preparation, based on Main 55e1970a5 and reviewed durability sections 15.6–15.9. No source, package, lock, test or gate change was made. Layout Source 27b153f3 remains independently reviewed; its approval and landing are prerequisites for dependent implementation.\n\nCurrent boundaries:\n1. HistorySource.page/retained (packages/replay/src/source.ts:44,53) receive byte/entry allowances. HTTP caps are 4 MiB per reply, 200 page entries and 30 seconds per read; contract native page and retained limits are 1 MiB (packages/contract/src/read.ts:23). The verifier charges successful reply bytes at verify.ts:520,559,623 and bounds 64 scopes, 100,000 entries, 256 MiB and foreign depth 16 at :65. These are distinct from native archive-pass admission limits.\n2. GitProgram supplies hardened argument-array execution and disables replacement/lazy fetching (packages/git/src/program.ts:97). repositorySource (:143) and objectId remain legacy SHA-1 contracts. nodeExec (node.ts:14) captures up to 1 GiB; it is not a bounded archive transport merely because a later parser checks a blob size.\n3. The portable replay main exports cli.ts; it currently constructs only HTTP source (cli.ts:64), and Io has no disk/Git ports (:25). The replay package has no Git dependency (package.json:18). Node-only imports must stay outside portable entrypoints. A new reviewed subpath/dependency, including the lockfile when required, is preferable to relative cross-package imports or codec duplication.\n4. The ordinary dap clone argv has no archive refspec (packages/cli/src/commands.ts:1320). Offline witnesses must actually bring refs/artroom/journal/\u003cnative scope ID\u003e into a real clone, rather than quietly populate a bare fixture and call it cloning.\n5. An unread target throws SourceError before a Report exists (verify.ts:443), while a missing retained input is incomplete (:559). No known head adds the existing service-head trust (:450); sourceName is native identity policy, not source provenance. Snapshot retention already preserves unwalked ancestry (:1109), and text bytes are checked under DOMAINS.text (:579). Receipt is the existing Receipt envelope with fact: FactRef (contract/src/entry.ts:166).\n\nProposed dependency order and decisions for checker:\nA. First a bounded explicit-format object transport and clone HistorySource, using the adopted v1 codecs after they land. Pin each exact scope ref to a commit once per read session, including incarnation; foreign scopes resolve only when the verifier names them. No working-tree path or fetch fallback. Metadata probes, stdout/stderr collection, object hashes, paths/modes, visited/cache state and time must be bounded before work. Decide exact per-read versus session accounting and lifecycle. A valid 8 MiB archive segment may exceed the 4 MiB HistorySource reply allowance: adopt conservative unavailability or a reviewed bounded streaming rule, never silently undercharge physical reads.\nB. Decide how a normal clone obtains archive refs: explicit local/refspec behavior and a real clone witness. This is separate from token minting, provider access and writer permission.\nC. Then add Node CLI ports/options --git, --texts and --receipt, with digest-only regular-file text lookup, bounded receipt parsing and no clone-derived filesystem joins. Decide whether --receipt accepts the full existing Receipt or a separately versioned fact-only form; do not guess aliases. Pin the selected commit and prove integrity/continuity before archived membership; validate an available shorter prefix before behind. Missing/corrupt/limited reads cannot become archived or fabricated Report facts.\nD. Resolve the proposal's “verify and judges do not change” against archive-head trust and the requirement to classify a noncommit/missing-head archive as mismatch. The current target-read contract cannot produce a Report with a real incarnation when no target history exists. Prefer a narrow explicit provenance/error boundary or separate archive-read diagnostic, subject to adoption; do not rewrite human trust strings or invent scope frames. Judges, journal bytes, replay rules and HTTP defaults remain unchanged.\nE. Compose the required four cutoff histories: declared genesis, outcome value, outcome snapshot with unwalked ancestry still incomplete, and observing delivery value. Compare real offline clone versus existing HTTP reports apart from adopted source trust; no service or anchor supplies the positive clone dependencies. Label synthetic admission and scripted capabilities honestly. Include changed/cut lines, wrong head, absent foreign ref, unsafe modes/paths and receipt equal/below/above cutoff.\n\nThis is preparation only. No producer, privacy certificate, G1 persisted closure/at-send retention lease, root outcome, publication, push or deployment is delivered.","body":{"no_git_artifact":"true","promise":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:604855bee23b69d2caa4687bdb416ab4fb04c0da","request":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8b467faae1b3e996471b70e5e8277627447e2cd0"}}